# Routes

Each feature is a folder under `apps/<app>/src/routes/`. Study a neighbor before adding one (`apps/bookmarks/src/routes/add` for forms, `apps/espresso/src/routes/notes/[id]` for a detail page).

## Server

- `load` in `+page.server.ts` returns the data the page renders. Missing records throw `error(404, '...')`
- Mutations are named form actions. Validate, then call the service. Failure is `fail(status, { error, ...fields })`. Success may `redirect`
- Keep prompts, API clients, and tokens in the server file. The page only receives typed data
- User-facing errors are short sentences. Log the underlying error with `console.error`

## Page

- `let { data }: { data: PageData } = $props()` and derive view values with `$derived`
- Forms use `method="POST"`, `action="?/create"`, and `use:enhance`. Restore fields from `form` when the action returns them
- Put a `<title>` in `<svelte:head>`
- In-app links go through `resolve()`. Cross-app links use the origins from `appUrls()`
- Page `<style>` is scoped. Use tokens. Short class names are fine here (`.note`, `.param`)

Site chrome is `MNBSiteFrame` from `@mnb/ui`, rendered by each app's root `+layout.svelte`. A new top-level section gets a link there.
